From: Leszek Swirski <leszeks@chromium.org>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 11:54:25 +0200
Subject: [M152] [deserializer] Check source hash before starting BG merge

Original change's description:
> [deserializer] Check source hash before starting BG merge
>
> Off-thread code cache deserialization happens before source text is
> available, so we can't verify the cache's source hash up front. When
> source text becomes available, SourceTextAvailable previously set up a
> background merge with a matching Script from the compilation cache
> without checking whether the serialized code cache's source hash
> (including module vs. classic origin options) matched the incoming
> script. If a module code cache was handed to a classic script load of
> the same URL, the background merge would merge incompatible scripts
> before FinishOffThreadDeserialize rejected the cache.
>
> Check the cached data's source hash via
> CodeSerializer::NotifySourceTextAvailable before setting up the
> background merge task, and record the result in
> OffThreadDeserializeData::source_sanity_check_result so
> FinishOffThreadDeserialize does not recompute it. Populate
> OffThreadDeserializeData in-place in StartDeserializeOffThread and avoid
> reading data->sanity_check_result or mutating cached_data->Reject() in
> NotifySourceTextAvailable so the main-thread source check cannot race
> with or be clobbered by concurrent background deserialization.
>
